---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/docs/Callout.astro";
import Endpoint from "../../components/docs/Endpoint.astro";
import Params from "../../components/docs/Params.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Connections" lead="A connection stores one provider credential, encrypted, for your agents to use. You pay your providers directly; Offhook adds nothing on top." slug="connections">
        <h2 id="providers">Supported providers</h2>
        <p>Each connection has a <code>provider_kind</code> and a <code>provider_name</code> from this list:</p>
        <div class="wd-table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Providers</th><th>Secret fields</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>stt</code></td><td><code>deepgram</code></td><td><code>api_key</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>tts</code></td><td><code>cartesia</code>, <code>openai</code></td><td><code>api_key</code>; Cartesia also takes <code>voice_id</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>llm</code></td><td><code>groq</code>, <code>gemini</code>, <code>openrouter</code>, <code>openai</code></td><td><code>api_key</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>telephony</code></td><td><code>plivo</code>, <code>twilio</code></td><td>Plivo: <code>auth_id</code>, <code>auth_token</code>, <code>from_number</code><br />Twilio: <code>account_sid</code>, <code>auth_token</code>, <code>from_number</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <Callout kind="note"><code>GET /v1/providers</code> returns the list your deployment supports.</Callout>

        <h2 id="create">Create a connection</h2>
        <Endpoint method="POST" path="/v1/connections" />
        <Params rows={[
          { name: "name", type: "string", required: true, desc: "A label for the connection. Must be unique within your tenant." },
          { name: "provider_kind", type: "string", required: true, desc: "One of <code>stt</code>, <code>tts</code>, <code>llm</code> or <code>telephony</code>." },
          { name: "provider_name", type: "string", required: true, desc: "A provider from the table above." },
          { name: "secrets", type: "object", required: true, desc: "The provider's secret fields from the table above. Never returned." },
        ]} />
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/connections \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "name": "my-plivo",
    "provider_kind": "telephony",
    "provider_name": "plivo",
    "secrets": {
      "auth_id": "MA…",
      "auth_token": "…",
      "from_number": "+14155550100"
    }
  }'` }, { label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "id": "6a1d3f8e-2c4b-4a9e-b7d1-0e5f3c8a2b61",
  "name": "my-plivo",
  "provider_kind": "telephony",
  "provider_name": "plivo",
  "created_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:00Z"
}` }]} />
        <p>Creating a connection with a name you already use returns <code>409</code>.</p>

        <h2 id="list">List and retrieve</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/connections" />
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/connections/{id}" />
        <p>Both return the fields shown above. Secrets are never included in any response.</p>

        <h2 id="update">Rotate a secret</h2>
        <Endpoint method="PATCH" path="/v1/connections/{id}" />
        <p>Send a new <code>secrets</code> object, a new <code>name</code>, or both. The new secret is encrypted in place, and agents using the connection pick it up on their next call.</p>

        <h2 id="delete">Delete a connection</h2>
        <Endpoint method="DELETE" path="/v1/connections/{id}" />
        <p>Returns <code>409</code> while an agent still uses the connection. Delete that agent first.</p>

</DocsLayout>
